      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The core economic principle of capital mobility is a powerful force, and it cannot be dismissed simply because a policy is politically desirable. When wealth is highly mobile, any tax that significantly targets it creates an immediate incentive for capital to move to jurisdictions with lower tax burdens. Therefore, the fiscal reality is that wealth taxes risk driving investment away unless they are paired with extremely robust international regulatory frameworks.",
      "source": "target",
